Dynamic texture registration reports a device that refused the allocation.

`register_dynamic_texture` on the platform window returned nothing, so a
`CreateTexture2D` that failed on DirectX left the window holding an id
over no texture: `update_user_texture` accepted every frame for it and
the chain sampled an unbound slot, which reads as black. The only trace
was the HRESULT `log_err` wrote. The platform call now returns
`Result<(), String>`, DirectX answers with the size it was refused (and
`unsupported` below the feature level, the same word the chain path
uses), and `Window::register_dynamic_texture` forgets the id and hands
the message to the caller, who already shows registration errors. Blade
and Metal don't fail here, so their windows wrap the call in `Ok`.

Diffed against the tree with every earlier gpui patch applied.

